# ML Evaluation & Fit Scenarios

**Code:** `src/train/diagnostics.py` (thresholds live there — keep this rule in sync).

Every training run must emit diagnostics JSON and specimen error tables. UI **Model results** tab must surface scenario severity.

## Scenarios (check all)

| Scenario | Detection | Severity |
|----------|-----------|----------|
| **good_fit** | test R² ≥ target, train-test R² gap < 0.05 | ok |
| **overfit** | train-test R² gap ≥ 0.05 | warn |
| **overfit_severe** | gap ≥ 0.10 | critical |
| **underfit** | train R² < 0.75 AND test R² below mode threshold | critical |
| **high_cv_variance** | CV RMSE std/mean ≥ 0.40 | warn (demoted if core fit is good) |
| **optimistic_holdout** | test RMSE / CV RMSE ≤ 0.55 | warn (demoted if core fit is good) |
| **pessimistic_holdout** | test RMSE / CV RMSE ≥ 1.45 | warn |
| **peak_outliers** | ≥20% of holdout specimens with >15% peak error | warn |
| **curve_poor_specimens** | ≥15% of test specimens with R² < 0.60 | warn |
| **curve_softening_miss** | ≥10% of specimens miss post-peak softening | warn |

Mode test R² floors: peak **0.80**, curve **0.82**. Good-fit targets: **0.88** both modes.

Rate-based specimen flags avoid false alarms on tiny PEER holdouts while still catching systemic failure.

## Required outputs (`outputs/`)

| File | Purpose |
|------|---------|
| `training_diagnostics_peak.json` | Scenario flags + recommendations |
| `training_diagnostics_curve.json` | Same for curve mode |
| `specimen_errors_peak.csv` | Per-specimen peak errors + outlier flag |
| `specimen_errors_curve.csv` | Per-specimen R², softening_miss, poor_fit |
| `metrics_*.csv` | train/test/CV columns for every model |

## Model selection (must follow)

1. Lowest **group CV RMSE** on training specimens
2. Penalize train-test R² gap > **0.05**
3. Do **not** pick a model with **underfit** or **overfit_severe** if another candidate is acceptable
4. Saved joblib is **refit on full data** after selection; holdout metrics come from pre-refit pipe

## Training features

- Use `TRAINING_FEATURE_COLUMNS` — **exclude** derived `axial_load_ratio`
- Regularized RF / XGB / MLP only (see `model_zoo()` in `service.py`)
- **Never** report test R² alone — always train R², gap, CV RMSE, specimen outliers

## Curve mode limits (document in UI/report)

Pointwise `(params + displacement) → load` **cannot** guarantee post-peak softening. Flag `curve_softening_miss`; do not claim full hysteresis/backbone fidelity without a sequence or monotonic model.

## When changing thresholds or scenarios

Update `diagnostics.py`, this rule, `apps/docs/guides/ml-pipeline.md`, and platform-guide Changelog in the same change.
